      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-17T18:22:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "MinApiLevelModuleController takes in an option of property name to get api level. So far it can be one of the 2 values:\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/android/tools/tradefederation/core/src/com/android/tradefed/testtype/suite/module/MinApiLevelModuleController.java?rcl\u003d79d857dd6347374c0dd1763d3f05f121d8ad4e5c\u0026l\u003d31\nand default value is ro.build.version.sdk.\n\nNot sure if we can come up with a more generic name?",
      "parentUuid": "c433587e_6da9a205",
      "revId": "c0f5af78e283c496698a8ee3f657b86c5771f6da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4eb6b168_adf2666f",
        "filename": "cc/test.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-17T18:25:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That link is the exact definition of an implementation detail.  _Why_ would a developer choose one over the other?  What are they trying to say about their test when they choose one?  For example, should this be two different properties, test_min_sdk_version and test_product_first_api_level?",
      "parentUuid": "64f6a60b_6ce21601",
      "revId": "c0f5af78e283c496698a8ee3f657b86c5771f6da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "63287833_b21e93cc",
        "filename": "cc/test.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1088076
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-17T18:35:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. If we want to make it more general, how about name it Test_device_prop? and one can set the value to any device property and potentially used in other preparer.\n\nIf we want the setting to be more specific to the use case, keep the name Api_level_prop maybe better, in case it needs to support a different property name.\nHaving 2 different properties like test_min_sdk_version and test_product_first_api_level works too, if soong team doesn\u0027t mind that this struct contains too many properties.",
      "parentUuid": "4eb6b168_adf2666f",
      "revId": "c0f5af78e283c496698a8ee3f657b86c5771f6da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b26e53d_ee0f9250",
        "filename": "cc/test.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 80,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-17T22:47:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Developers writing tests should not have to know the name of the property on the device that sets the SDK version, and if the cost of that is having multiple properties in Soong then I\u0027m fine with that.",
      "parentUuid": "63287833_b21e93cc",
      "revId": "c0f5af78e283c496698a8ee3f657b86c5771f6da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3c72ab7_e5af92bf",
        "filename": "cc/test.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
